{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"569528855e4e3f3384f8c5ae2b215443c0dc7edd7b8267548458ea6a40a1903f","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review / code-review gate calibration","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py","code_review_result_v1","plan_review_result_v1","REVIEW_RESULT","IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION","code-v2","code-v3","ADR-0036","docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/g7-promotion-path.md","G7 leaf-plan parent-containment criterion","norm_id","CLAUDE.md","remediation_mode","novelty rising floor","d4cf","b9c0","9f25","a8e5","74d9","f32e"],"problem_keywords":["code-review calibration","blocking threshold","advisory remediation","completion-verifier","plan-review gate","leaf-parent scope drift","verdict instability","non-convergent gate","serious-tier findings","measurement framework","advisory uptake","new-code grounding gap"],"propositions":["Code review is too loose: zero blocking finding votes across 162 changes because no real finding reached the 0.95 threshold, so a data-driven block threshold is derived and enabled for serious-tier criteria.","Agent guidance mandating remediation of all valid plan-review advisories is loosened to judgment so organic advisory uptake can be measured.","Completion-verifier FAIL verdicts are not durably persisted, ratchet piecemeal, and signed-children epic ACs defeat the certifiable:false escape hatch.","A new plan-review criterion (G7) gates leaf-plan scope containment against the parent plan, firing at the claim-gating review so leaf drift is caught ticket-by-ticket instead of at epic close.","A measurement-framework artifact records the pre-change baseline plus re-runnable queries for post-change code-review block counts and plan-review norm_id advisory-survival, with multi-day field telemetry deferred to the next calibration session.","Field finding: plan-review claim gate showed verdict instability and apparent non-convergence, later attributed mainly to agent-introduced plan inaccuracies; the gate is high-precision and converges when plans are made code-accurate, with residual new-code grounding INDETERMINATE and one-test-per-round blast-radius friction."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785204177630481061,"uuid":"9fd13891-1924-4d28-ba1b-8c51b9b8e342"}